1
00:00:33,314 --> 00:00:35,009
Five...

2
00:00:35,082 --> 00:00:37,414
nine, ten, eleven...

3
00:00:37,485 --> 00:00:39,385
twelve, thirteen,
nineteen, seventeen...

4
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,500
Arnie, eat some chicken.

5
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,400
I don't want any chicken, Gilbert.

6
00:00:46,627 --> 00:00:49,027
You want some corn?

7
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:52,100
- I want some corn.
- Have some corn.

8
00:00:57,905 --> 00:00:59,338
Good?

9
00:01:01,609 --> 00:01:03,201
Not good corn.

10
00:01:07,681 --> 00:01:09,876
Gilbert...

11
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:11,474
are they gonna come soon?

12
00:01:11,552 --> 00:01:14,544
'Cause I gotta go back home,
you know?

13
00:01:14,622 --> 00:01:16,249
Pretty soon.

14
00:01:16,323 --> 00:01:18,257
I want them to come.

15
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,558
- You wanna go home?
- No.

16
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:24,564
I wanna see 'em.

17
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:29,400
They're gonna come soon, huh?

18
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,197
How many more miles
till they come, Gilbert?

19
00:01:32,273 --> 00:01:33,900
- Three million, buddy.
- Three?

20
00:01:33,974 --> 00:01:35,601
- Yep.
- Okay.

21
00:01:44,985 --> 00:01:47,818
That's them, huh?
Look, it's them!

22
00:01:48,956 --> 00:01:51,254
Look! Look over there!

23
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,300
Look at them, Gilbert!
They're coming!

24
00:02:08,008 --> 00:02:10,636
Honk your horn!
Honk your horn!

25
00:02:14,315 --> 00:02:16,681
My brother Arnie's
about to turn 18.

26
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:20,200
My family's planning
a big party for him.

27
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:25,000
Watching the campers
is our yearly ritual.

28
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:29,600
They're doing the right thing
just passing through.

29
00:02:32,166 --> 00:02:34,225
God, Arnie.
You're gettin' so big.

30
00:02:34,301 --> 00:02:37,464
Pretty soon, I ain't gonna
be able to carry you no more.

31
00:02:37,538 --> 00:02:40,632
You know,
you're getting littler, Gilbert.

32
00:02:40,708 --> 00:02:43,336
You're getting littler.
You're shrinking.

33
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,700
You're shrinking, Gilbert.

34
00:02:59,526 --> 00:03:01,255
Endora.

35
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,300
Endora's where we are.

36
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:08,400
Describing Endora
is like dancing to no music.

37
00:03:09,303 --> 00:03:12,204
It's a town where
nothing much ever happens...

38
00:03:12,273 --> 00:03:14,673
and nothing much ever will.

39
00:03:16,677 --> 00:03:19,669
Lamson's Grocery is where I work.

40
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:23,900
And miles out of town on
the interstate, there's Foodland...

41
00:03:24,084 --> 00:03:26,279
where everyone else shops.

42
00:03:27,721 --> 00:03:29,746
This is where I live
with my family.

43
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:35,100
My dad built the house, and it's
my job to keep up the repairs.

44
00:03:37,031 --> 00:03:40,228
Doctors said we'd be lucky
if Arnie lived to be ten.

45
00:03:40,301 --> 00:03:42,963
Well, ten came and went.
Now the doctors are saying...

46
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:46,500
"Any time now.
Arnie can go at any time."

47
00:03:58,385 --> 00:04:01,786
- Some days you want him to live...
- The head.

48
00:04:01,855 --> 00:04:03,447
...some days you don't.

49
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:06,600
- What is it, buddy?
- I killed him.

50
00:04:10,597 --> 00:04:13,623
- I killed him, Gilbert.
- I know.

51
00:04:13,701 --> 00:04:15,396
I know, buddy.

52
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:25,000
My older sister Amy's
more like a mother.

53
00:04:25,279 --> 00:04:29,181
She used to manage the elementary
school cafeteria over in Motley...

54
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:31,900
until it burned down last year.

55
00:04:34,088 --> 00:04:36,079
My other sister, Ellen,
just turned 15.

56
00:04:36,156 --> 00:04:40,149
She got her braces off, and she's
been walking around going "Ooh, ah."

57
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:43,700
Like she can't believe
the feel of teeth.

58
00:04:50,237 --> 00:04:53,604
I got another brother, Larry,
but he got away.

59
00:04:53,674 --> 00:04:55,938
And then there's Mama,
who in her day...

60
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:58,376
was the prettiest girl
in these parts.

61
00:04:58,445 --> 00:05:01,437
Ever since our dad
was hung out to dry 17 years ago...

62
00:05:01,515 --> 00:05:03,380
Mama's had her hands full.

63
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:07,700
You see, with Mama there's
no nice way to break it to you.

64
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:11,600
She hasn't left the house
in over seven years.

65
00:05:13,761 --> 00:05:16,025
- I'm Gilbert.
- Ellen, I need your help.

66
00:05:16,096 --> 00:05:19,190
- What is it?
- Gilbert Grape.

67
00:05:22,770 --> 00:05:25,967
Sunshine? Where's my sunshine?

68
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,031
I don't know, Mama.

69
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:30,700
- Just the essentials.
- Okay.

70
00:05:34,081 --> 00:05:37,141
Gilbert, get him down from there.

71
00:05:38,852 --> 00:05:40,979
- Hurry.
- Let's go.

72
00:05:42,256 --> 00:05:45,987
- Amy, have you seen Arnie?
- No.

73
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:48,300
I thought he was with you.

74
00:05:49,663 --> 00:05:51,995
I wonder where he is.

75
00:05:52,066 --> 00:05:53,897
Gee, I don't know.

76
00:05:53,967 --> 00:05:55,901
Ellen, have you seen your brother?

77
00:05:55,969 --> 00:05:58,802
He's in the tree.

78
00:05:58,872 --> 00:06:02,239
He is not in the tree.
Gilbert already looked in the tree.

79
00:06:02,309 --> 00:06:05,176
Isn't that right, Gilbert?

80
00:06:05,245 --> 00:06:06,837
Yeah, that's right.

81
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:14,500
Don't do that. You scared me.
Come here.

82
00:06:16,990 --> 00:06:19,049
- I was up there!
- Yeah, you were up in the tree.

83
00:06:19,126 --> 00:06:21,060
I was right up there.

84
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:13,300
Can I help you with anything?

85
00:07:15,448 --> 00:07:17,507
Thank you, and good-bye.

86
00:07:21,554 --> 00:07:23,215
- Gilbert?
- Sir?

87
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:25,554
Is something goin' on at Foodland?

88
00:07:25,625 --> 00:07:30,085
I wouldn't know, sir.
I don't shop there. I'd rather die.

89
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:34,800
I'll tell you, Foodland's
up to something if you ask me.

90
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:42,300
It's those lobsters, isn't it?

91
00:07:42,575 --> 00:07:45,442
Scads of lobsters all in a tank.

92
00:07:45,512 --> 00:07:47,207
Am I right?

93
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:50,408
You know,
you shouldn't worry about it.

94
00:07:50,483 --> 00:07:54,078
It's just a phase. People
will come back here, believe me.

95
00:07:54,154 --> 00:07:56,145
- You think?
- Oh, yeah.

96
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:04,200
The way you say that makes me think
I'm talking to your father.

97
00:08:10,170 --> 00:08:12,400
- Can I have these two?
- No, just one.

98
00:08:12,472 --> 00:08:14,406
- Can I have these two?
- Sure, go ahead.

99
00:08:14,474 --> 00:08:16,305
Say "Thank you."

100
00:08:16,376 --> 00:08:18,657
- Say hello to Mama for me.
- All right. See you tomorrow.

101
00:08:18,712 --> 00:08:22,113
Gilbert? That was Mrs. Carver
needing a delivery.

102
00:08:22,182 --> 00:08:24,878
Could you?

103
00:08:32,792 --> 00:08:34,623
Boys, go on outside.

104
00:08:34,694 --> 00:08:37,663
- But we don't want to.
- Yeah, we don't want to.

105
00:08:37,731 --> 00:08:38,925
Go play.

106
00:08:45,472 --> 00:08:48,168
Get back in the truck.
Keep countin', okay?

107
00:08:48,241 --> 00:08:52,234
Okay. I was counting.

108
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:22,800
Five, ten, eleven, twelve, thirteen,
fourteen, fifteen, sixteen...

109
00:09:30,116 --> 00:09:31,481
Hey, kids, let's play!

110
00:09:31,551 --> 00:09:33,985
Come on!

111
00:09:34,053 --> 00:09:37,955
We got the trampoline.
Come on, boys. It's fun!

112
00:09:42,362 --> 00:09:44,592
The ice cream's gonna melt...

113
00:09:44,664 --> 00:09:46,097
soon.

114
00:09:49,135 --> 00:09:52,627
You're right.
It is melting.

115
00:10:27,307 --> 00:10:29,275
Oh, my God!

116
00:10:32,879 --> 00:10:35,746
- Oh, my.
- Oh, my God.

117
00:10:38,952 --> 00:10:41,614
- Come on up. I wanna show you.
- I don't wanna do it.

118
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:45,100
- You don't wanna do it?
- I want a pool.

119
00:10:45,792 --> 00:10:48,226
- You want a pool?
- Yeah, we want a pool.

120
00:10:48,294 --> 00:10:50,626
Come on up.
Up, up, up, up.

121
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:00,900
Gilbert was just making a delivery.

122
00:11:05,778 --> 00:11:09,043
Gilbert, come here for a second.

123
00:11:17,257 --> 00:11:20,317
- Here.
- Oh, no, really.

124
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:23,600
Oh, no, here.
I insist. You deserve it.

125
00:11:26,366 --> 00:11:27,765
Thank you.

126
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:30,200
- Thank you.
- Bye, Gilbert.

127
00:11:32,872 --> 00:11:35,534
Come by my office.

128
00:11:35,608 --> 00:11:37,508
We need to talk.

129
00:11:56,663 --> 00:12:00,064
Okay, son, it's a little dangerous
up there. Come on down.

130
00:12:00,133 --> 00:12:01,600
Arnie, get down!

131
00:12:01,668 --> 00:12:03,602
Come on, son.
We've had enough fun for one day.

132
00:12:03,670 --> 00:12:05,262
Come on down.

133
00:12:13,179 --> 00:12:16,080
- Son?
- Yeah?

134
00:12:16,149 --> 00:12:19,016
- Come on down.
- No!

135
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:22,400
I'm not coming down!
I'm goin' up there!

136
00:12:22,555 --> 00:12:25,285
Son, come on down.

137
00:12:25,358 --> 00:12:27,292
I'm gonna go up there!

138
00:12:29,696 --> 00:12:32,688
- Come on down, buddy.
- Look up here.

139
00:12:32,765 --> 00:12:34,630
Hi!

140
00:12:36,202 --> 00:12:38,602
Okay, son.
Come on down.

141
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,800
I'm gonna go up here!

142
00:12:42,275 --> 00:12:43,435
Come on, son.

143
00:12:43,509 --> 00:12:46,910
I'm goin' higher than before!

144
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,345
I'm goin' high!

145
00:12:48,414 --> 00:12:52,009
It's gonna be getting dark soon.
Come on down.

146
00:12:52,085 --> 00:12:54,679
Hey, Bob.
Yeah, here we go again.

147
00:12:54,754 --> 00:12:57,780
Basically, I don't like
to work on carburetors...

148
00:12:57,857 --> 00:12:59,950
and I can tell
without gettin' into it...

149
00:13:00,026 --> 00:13:03,154
that that is a complicated unit.

150
00:13:03,229 --> 00:13:07,393
I understand. I can do it myself,
but I need the part.

151
00:13:07,467 --> 00:13:09,332
Look, let me show you.

152
00:13:09,402 --> 00:13:11,734
See, it's this
little guy right here.

153
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,100
The needle valve is worn down.

154
00:13:14,273 --> 00:13:16,867
I need a new one.
Can we order it?

155
00:13:16,942 --> 00:13:18,409
Yes, ma'am.

156
00:13:18,477 --> 00:13:22,277
- I can order it.
- How long will that take?

157
00:13:22,348 --> 00:13:25,112
- Probably a week.
- A week?

158
00:13:25,184 --> 00:13:26,947
Don't make us come get you.

159
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:31,100
You don't have to come get me!
I'm goin' up here!

160
00:13:35,127 --> 00:13:37,288
I'm not gonna fall!

161
00:13:44,803 --> 00:13:46,737
My shoe done fell off.

162
00:13:53,646 --> 00:13:56,774
I know a boy whose name is Arnie.

163
00:13:56,849 --> 00:14:00,910
He's about to turn 18
and have a big party

164
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,800
I know a boy whose name is Arnie.

165
00:14:06,592 --> 00:14:09,152
Come on down, buddy.
Come on.

166
00:14:15,968 --> 00:14:18,732
Match in the gas tank Boom, boom.

167
00:14:39,325 --> 00:14:43,125
Good boy.
Come on down, buddy.

168
00:14:57,710 --> 00:15:00,679
Here we go. Thanks a lot, Jerry.
Really sorry.

169
00:15:00,746 --> 00:15:03,579
Good boy. Good boy.

170
00:15:03,649 --> 00:15:06,812
I'm gonna take him home.
I promise it won't happen again.

171
00:15:06,885 --> 00:15:09,649
We hear this every time.
Then after a couple of days...

172
00:15:09,722 --> 00:15:11,656
he's right back up there again.

173
00:15:11,724 --> 00:15:14,852
But this is the last time.
Right, buddy?

174
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,400
- It's the last time.
- Yeah.

175
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:22,800
- Come on. Let's go.
- I wanna go back up there again.

176
00:15:25,971 --> 00:15:28,997
- I wanna go up there again.
- Arnie, man, good job.

177
00:15:29,074 --> 00:15:31,542
Don't touch him.

178
00:15:31,610 --> 00:15:34,010
Way to go, Arnie.
Could you do it again for me?

179
00:15:34,079 --> 00:15:36,013
Get out of here.

180
00:15:36,081 --> 00:15:38,515
Could you help me out later
with the fridge?

181
00:15:38,584 --> 00:15:41,382
- With the what?
- Something wrong with the fridge.

182
00:15:41,453 --> 00:15:43,978
- The electricity?
- I don't know. Maybe.

183
00:15:44,056 --> 00:15:46,752
All right.
I have to get my tools.

184
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:51,100
I'll just come by later.
You be careful, all right?

185
00:15:56,500 --> 00:16:00,100
Don't disappear like that
again on me, okay?

186
00:16:03,142 --> 00:16:05,906
I disappeared on Mom like that.

187
00:16:05,978 --> 00:16:09,072
- Please don't disappear.
- Just let him go.

188
00:16:09,148 --> 00:16:11,446
- Will you bring the milk?
- I promise, Mama.

189
00:16:11,517 --> 00:16:14,145
Good boy. Good boy.

190
00:16:15,387 --> 00:16:16,979
The food.

191
00:16:20,993 --> 00:16:22,654
Are we ready
to talk about the party?

192
00:16:22,728 --> 00:16:26,129
- Sure.
- Ellen's in charge of decorations.

193
00:16:26,198 --> 00:16:27,790
Purple, orange and green.

194
00:16:27,866 --> 00:16:29,197
- Sounds good.
- Theme colors.

195
00:16:29,268 --> 00:16:31,202
That sounds pretty good.

196
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,800
I'm doing the food, the cake.

197
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:38,300
Arnie, I'm making something
very special for you.

198
00:16:38,410 --> 00:16:40,537
And Mama,
you can supervise everything.

199
00:16:40,612 --> 00:16:43,274
- Okay with everybody?
- That's disgusting.

200
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,900
- Sounds good.
- What about me?

201
00:16:46,585 --> 00:16:48,951
You are the guest of honor.
How about that?

202
00:16:49,021 --> 00:16:51,854
What about me?
It's my party!

203
00:16:51,924 --> 00:16:53,755
You just show up, buddy.
That's your job.

204
00:16:53,826 --> 00:16:56,386
- All you have to do is show up.
- You don't have to do anything.

205
00:16:56,395 --> 00:16:59,262
All you have to do is turn 18.

206
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:02,100
You know, that just leaves Gilbert.

207
00:17:02,201 --> 00:17:04,761
You're the only one
without anything to do.

208
00:17:04,837 --> 00:17:06,828
- Got any ideas?
- Sure he does.

209
00:17:06,905 --> 00:17:09,635
- No, I don't.
- Yes, you do.

210
00:17:09,708 --> 00:17:12,176
I'm almost 16,
and I've got pages of ideas.

211
00:17:12,244 --> 00:17:15,645
She designed a whole cake,
and you haven't done anything.

212
00:17:15,714 --> 00:17:18,012
- Stop it, Ellen.
- Can I be excused?

213
00:17:18,083 --> 00:17:22,315
- He never does anything!
- Can't we do something as a family?

214
00:17:22,388 --> 00:17:24,356
- This is no fair!
- Can I please be excused?

215
00:17:24,423 --> 00:17:28,917
- We're planning this as a family.
- It's my party though!

216
00:17:28,994 --> 00:17:33,829
So it's gonna be an exact copy of
the original they built in Boone.

217
00:17:33,899 --> 00:17:36,333
- Really?
- Which is no big deal.

218
00:17:36,402 --> 00:17:40,031
All Burger Barns
are built identical.

219
00:17:40,105 --> 00:17:42,539
They're prefabricated.
They just ship 'em out.

220
00:17:42,608 --> 00:17:44,940
It's so efficient.
It's amazing.

221
00:17:45,010 --> 00:17:47,103
In a matter of a couple days...

222
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:50,200
there can be
a whole new restaurant.

223
00:17:50,349 --> 00:17:53,079
So I was driving past
the building site today.

224
00:17:53,152 --> 00:17:57,054
You know, it's goin' up
right down the road from Foodland.

225
00:17:57,122 --> 00:17:59,716
The general manager was there.
So I says...

226
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:03,400
"Can I fill out an application?"
He said, "You bet you can."

227
00:18:03,562 --> 00:18:05,689
So I did, you know,
and it looks really good.

228
00:18:05,764 --> 00:18:09,393
I might be wearin' one of them
uniforms, flippin' some burgers...

229
00:18:09,468 --> 00:18:12,631
saltin' some fries.

230
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:18,400
You never know. It could be the
best thing that ever happened to me.

231
00:18:19,611 --> 00:18:21,306
Get out of here!

232
00:18:23,148 --> 00:18:24,740
I saw her!

233
00:18:26,985 --> 00:18:29,613
- That wasn't nice.
- What? What did I do?

234
00:18:29,688 --> 00:18:31,553
You know what you did.

235
00:18:31,623 --> 00:18:34,285
That's your mother in there.

236
00:18:34,359 --> 00:18:36,418
- Your mother.
- I know.

237
00:18:38,697 --> 00:18:41,188
I don't get you, man.
I just don't get it.

238
00:18:41,266 --> 00:18:43,791
- Let's go, buddy.
- Okay.

239
00:18:43,869 --> 00:18:46,235
Come on.

240
00:18:46,305 --> 00:18:48,899
Run, now! Run!

241
00:18:51,610 --> 00:18:54,477
- Bye-bye, Mama.
- Bye, you guys.

242
00:19:15,934 --> 00:19:18,767
I'm not tired yet, Gilbert.

243
00:19:19,838 --> 00:19:21,635
Gotta go to sleep, okay?

244
00:19:21,707 --> 00:19:24,232
Okay. Good-bye.

245
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:27,600
No, it's not good-bye.
It's good night.

246
00:19:28,447 --> 00:19:31,610
Good-bye is for when
you're going away.

247
00:19:31,683 --> 00:19:33,617
And we're not going anywhere,
are we?

248
00:19:33,685 --> 00:19:35,585
I know that.

249
00:19:35,654 --> 00:19:37,815
- Jeez, I know that, Gilbert.
- See you tomorrow.

250
00:19:37,890 --> 00:19:41,053
We're not going anywhere!

251
00:19:41,994 --> 00:19:43,222
Good-bye!

252
00:19:55,006 --> 00:19:56,906
- You gotta work later?
- Yeah, I do.

253
00:19:56,975 --> 00:19:58,670
Hi there, ladies.

254
00:19:58,744 --> 00:20:01,645
- I gotta come back.
- How's Mama?

255
00:20:01,713 --> 00:20:04,910
- She's fat.
- Come on, man.

256
00:20:04,983 --> 00:20:07,474
- She's not all that big.
- What?

257
00:20:07,552 --> 00:20:11,852
I saw a guy at the state fair
who was a little bit bigger.

258
00:20:11,923 --> 00:20:13,914
A little bit bigger?

259
00:20:13,992 --> 00:20:16,517
All I'm saying is she's not
the biggest I've ever seen.

260
00:20:16,595 --> 00:20:19,120
- Tucker, she's a whale!
- Take her out for a walk.

261
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:23,300
- Take her out for a jog.
- Tucker, she's a whale!

262
00:20:25,203 --> 00:20:27,967
- I'm just sayin' give her a chance.
- Hi, guys.

263
00:20:28,039 --> 00:20:31,338
- How's business?
- Not good.

264
00:20:31,410 --> 00:20:33,469
Nobody's dying.

265
00:20:33,545 --> 00:20:37,311
There's a clear ladder.
There's a clear corporate ladder.

266
00:20:37,382 --> 00:20:40,180
- I mean, this is not...
- That's good.

267
00:20:40,252 --> 00:20:42,447
That's a good thing for you to do.

268
00:20:42,521 --> 00:20:44,819
If you guys would give it a chance...

269
00:20:44,890 --> 00:20:48,257
I just was saying that it wasn't
something I should be doing myself.

270
00:20:48,326 --> 00:20:50,021
They use canola oil, okay?

271
00:20:50,095 --> 00:20:52,120
You know what canola oil is?
You probably don't.

272
00:20:52,197 --> 00:20:54,461
They probably don't sell it
at Lamson's Grocery.

273
00:20:54,533 --> 00:20:58,299
It's cutting edge.
It creates a crispier french fry...

274
00:20:58,370 --> 00:21:01,305
and a more unique product.

275
00:21:01,373 --> 00:21:04,865
And Burger Barn... Forget Wendy's,
Burger King, McDonald's.

276
00:21:04,943 --> 00:21:07,571
That's old hat.
Burger Barn's cutting edge.

277
00:21:07,646 --> 00:21:10,080
I mean,
I could really stand behind it.

278
00:21:10,148 --> 00:21:13,379
It's an innovative place.
They created the salad bar...

279
00:21:13,452 --> 00:21:18,082
which is now mimicked by every
single fast-food chain in America.

280
00:21:18,156 --> 00:21:19,680
They came up with that.

281
00:21:19,758 --> 00:21:23,922
Fifteen different toppings for
each salad, two kinds of lettuce.

282
00:21:23,995 --> 00:21:27,522
And it's all that you care to eat.

283
00:21:28,567 --> 00:21:32,594
You either go from clerk to fry cook
to cook to assistant manager...

284
00:21:32,671 --> 00:21:35,504
of you can go from clerk
to cashier captain...

285
00:21:35,574 --> 00:21:37,132
to assistant manager.

286
00:21:37,209 --> 00:21:41,202
And then from assistant manager,
you could go to manager...

287
00:21:41,279 --> 00:21:44,373
and then regional manager
and then...

288
00:21:52,958 --> 00:21:55,825
Look at the little fellas.

289
00:21:55,894 --> 00:21:57,987
You mean my hoppers.

290
00:21:58,063 --> 00:21:59,997
Let's try this.

291
00:22:00,065 --> 00:22:01,657
For my friend.

292
00:22:04,870 --> 00:22:07,065
There you go, my boy.

293
00:22:07,138 --> 00:22:09,868
What do you say, Arnie?

294
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:13,500
Thank you.
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

295
00:22:22,721 --> 00:22:24,416
This Thursday.

296
00:22:26,658 --> 00:22:29,491
It's our anniversary.

297
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:06,800
I'll need a delivery later.

298
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:17,304
Have a nice day.

299
00:23:24,416 --> 00:23:26,850
He's behind the chips.

300
00:23:29,688 --> 00:23:31,815
- Delivery, son.
- Excuse me?

301
00:23:31,900 --> 00:23:35,400
Delivery. She's gonna be
needin' some help.

302
00:23:36,227 --> 00:23:38,195
Yes, sir.

303
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,200
- Is that your bike?
- Yes.

304
00:23:42,334 --> 00:23:44,268
I'll do it, Gilbert.

305
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:52,400
- Here. Wait a sec.
- I got it!

306
00:23:54,312 --> 00:23:56,371
- I did it, huh?
- Look there.

307
00:23:56,448 --> 00:23:58,313
I did it by myself.

308
00:23:58,383 --> 00:24:01,910
Yeah. Look at that.

309
00:24:16,001 --> 00:24:18,128
I could go at any time.

310
00:24:20,972 --> 00:24:22,496
Any time.

311
00:24:24,743 --> 00:24:26,711
Excuse me. Where to?

312
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:28,900
Just keep going straight.

313
00:24:30,582 --> 00:24:32,174
All right.

314
00:24:33,852 --> 00:24:36,787
My mom wants me to become 18.

315
00:24:36,855 --> 00:24:40,256
I'm having a big party, huh?

316
00:24:40,325 --> 00:24:43,624
- When is that party coming?
- Six days.

317
00:24:43,700 --> 00:24:47,500
Six days and my party,
and I'm gonna become 18.

318
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:50,200
I'm 18, and you're not invited.

319
00:24:51,202 --> 00:24:53,602
- Don't be rude.
- It's okay.

320
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:56,700
He's just being honest.
I don't mind.

321
00:25:06,184 --> 00:25:08,914
- I got the groceries!
- Be careful with them.

322
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:12,000
I got the groceries.
I got 'em, okay?

323
00:25:16,695 --> 00:25:19,789
- I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.
- It's okay.

324
00:25:19,900 --> 00:25:23,800
- Don't worry about it.
- No, I'm really sorry.

325
00:25:24,202 --> 00:25:26,033
It's okay.

326
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:28,700
- I'm sorry.
- Don't be sorry.

327
00:25:29,140 --> 00:25:30,607
Are you sorry?

328
00:25:33,311 --> 00:25:35,677
I'm not sorry. He's not sorry.
We're not sorry.

329
00:25:35,747 --> 00:25:37,977
Don't be sorry.

330
00:25:38,049 --> 00:25:40,415
I'm not sorry.

331
00:25:45,223 --> 00:25:48,249
If people are gonna come that early,
we should have some appetizers.

332
00:25:48,326 --> 00:25:51,454
That'd be good. You know
those little Vienna sausage things?

333
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:55,700
You put 'em in grape jelly
and ketchup and make a sauce.

334
00:25:55,833 --> 00:25:57,994
- I want hot dogs, Mom.
- How about pretzels?

335
00:25:58,069 --> 00:26:01,334
You know, like those Hawaiian
appetizers they make with...

336
00:26:01,405 --> 00:26:03,339
You get pineapple chunks
out of the can...

337
00:26:03,407 --> 00:26:06,035
and you wrap them with
little pieces of bacon...

338
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:08,900
- and put a toothpick through 'em.
- How do you cook the bacon?

339
00:26:09,046 --> 00:26:10,536
In the oven on a pan.

340
00:26:10,615 --> 00:26:14,107
The bacon's not gonna be crisp if
you bake it in the oven on a sheet.

341
00:26:14,185 --> 00:26:16,312
- Yes, it will.
- Nobody wants greasy...

342
00:26:16,387 --> 00:26:19,117
- I want hot dogs!
- ...floppy bacon.

343
00:26:19,190 --> 00:26:22,853
- I want hot dogs!
- We're gonna have hot dogs, honey.

344
00:26:22,927 --> 00:26:26,124
I promise,
we're gonna have hot dogs.

345
00:26:26,197 --> 00:26:30,634
The thing about every party
that I've been to is that... What?

346
00:26:30,701 --> 00:26:33,295
Could you not talk
with your mouth full?

347
00:26:33,371 --> 00:26:34,668
Excuse me?

348
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:38,300
You're making me sick.
I'm gonna throw up.

349
00:26:39,076 --> 00:26:40,805
Okay, Dad.

350
00:26:42,113 --> 00:26:44,274
- Sure thing, Dad.
- Will you two cut it out?

351
00:26:44,348 --> 00:26:47,340
- Okay, Dad. Sure thing, Dad.
- That's nice.

352
00:26:47,500 --> 00:26:50,900
- Stop it, you guys.
- Dad's dead, Ellen.

353
00:26:51,222 --> 00:26:54,089
- I can't believe you said that.
- Shut up!

354
00:26:54,158 --> 00:26:55,591
Dad's dead!

355
00:26:55,700 --> 00:26:57,700
- Arnie...
- Dad's dead!

356
00:26:58,830 --> 00:27:02,357
Arnie, it's okay.
Stop it now.

357
00:27:02,500 --> 00:27:05,500
- Oh, God.
- Dad's dead! Dad's dead!

358
00:27:05,636 --> 00:27:08,764
- Mama, don't get upset.
- Make him stop.

359
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:11,104
- Arnie, shut up!
- Dead! Dead! Dead!

360
00:27:11,175 --> 00:27:13,871
- You're crazy, Arnie!
- Stop it.

361
00:27:17,949 --> 00:27:20,247
- Just calm down.
- Stop it!

362
00:27:20,318 --> 00:27:22,946
- Stop it!
- That's enough!

363
00:27:23,020 --> 00:27:25,215
Arnie, that's enough!

364
00:27:25,289 --> 00:27:28,258
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

365
00:27:28,326 --> 00:27:31,090
- Arnie, be quiet.
- Dad's dead!

366
00:27:31,162 --> 00:27:33,722
I said, stop it right now!

367
00:27:36,601 --> 00:27:38,660
It should be two-by-tens
or two-by-twelves...

368
00:27:38,736 --> 00:27:41,136
and the space
between 'em here should...

369
00:27:41,205 --> 00:27:43,571
Right now, it's at two feet.

370
00:27:43,641 --> 00:27:46,007
This should be 16 inches.
I mean, that's just standard.

371
00:27:46,077 --> 00:27:49,808
And this right here...
See this here? Flat flooring?

372
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:54,500
Once the wood gets old,
you're gonna fall right through it.

373
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:58,000
I guess Daddy wasn't
much of a carpenter.

374
00:27:58,700 --> 00:28:03,400
Gilbert, why did he use
two-by-sixes instead of two-by...

375
00:28:03,594 --> 00:28:05,789
- What?
- Keep it down.

376
00:28:05,863 --> 00:28:07,421
Sorry.

377
00:28:18,500 --> 00:28:20,700
She's coming.
She's coming.

378
00:28:40,031 --> 00:28:41,726
You all right?
You okay?

379
00:28:41,799 --> 00:28:43,767
Yeah, I'm fine.

380
00:28:43,834 --> 00:28:45,358
Thanks a lot for coming.

381
00:28:45,436 --> 00:28:48,166
I'll come by tomorrow
with the wood.

382
00:28:48,239 --> 00:28:50,799
Let's keep it quiet.
I forgot to tell you.

383
00:28:50,875 --> 00:28:52,536
- What?
- Burger Barn.

384
00:28:52,610 --> 00:28:54,635
I'm in. I got the call.

385
00:28:54,712 --> 00:28:57,579
- Good.
- It's not too late, you know.

386
00:28:57,648 --> 00:28:58,876
Good night.

387
00:29:01,852 --> 00:29:03,285
I think she's asleep.

388
00:29:03,354 --> 00:29:07,654
Say you wanna slice down zucchini
squash in the food dehydrator.

389
00:29:07,725 --> 00:29:10,353
- Look at this.
- Wonderful!

390
00:29:10,428 --> 00:29:14,228
- Perfect slices every time. Nice?
- Marvelous.

391
00:29:14,298 --> 00:29:16,823
'Course, if you know someone
that can't chew too well...

392
00:29:16,901 --> 00:29:18,698
take the corn off the cob.

393
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:23,300
Look at this. We'll just
turn down the dial a little...

394
00:29:26,811 --> 00:29:29,780
...freeze corn and sit there
for hours with a knife...

395
00:29:29,847 --> 00:29:31,439
literally hours,
cutting their corn.

396
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:34,600
- Unbelievable!
- 'Course, for un...

397
00:29:37,555 --> 00:29:40,956
- Right now, you get the...
- What are you doing?

398
00:29:41,025 --> 00:29:43,459
- Give me that.
- Sorry, Mama.

399
00:29:43,527 --> 00:29:44,960
Jeez.

400
00:29:46,297 --> 00:29:51,325
The $30 Dial-O-Matic Food Slicer,
a $ 160 value, right now.

401
00:29:51,500 --> 00:29:53,800
I made up that bed for you.

402
00:29:54,872 --> 00:29:56,601
What for?

403
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,800
Just in case you wanted a change.

404
00:30:01,379 --> 00:30:04,007
I'm happy right where I am.

405
00:30:04,081 --> 00:30:07,448
- You sure?
- Yeah.

406
00:30:20,798 --> 00:30:22,390
Here you go.

407
00:30:26,604 --> 00:30:28,697
Here you go, Mama.

408
00:30:28,773 --> 00:30:30,263
Thanks, kids.

409
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:33,700
- Good night, Mama.
- You're so helpful.

410
00:30:41,185 --> 00:30:43,710
I took her delivery,
we talked a little bit.

411
00:30:43,788 --> 00:30:45,722
And that was it.
I dropped her off.

412
00:30:45,790 --> 00:30:47,985
What's she doing here?

413
00:30:48,059 --> 00:30:49,924
I don't know.
She's just sort of here.

414
00:30:49,994 --> 00:30:51,723
I think their car broke down.

415
00:30:51,796 --> 00:30:53,559
Come on.
I see it in your face.

416
00:30:53,631 --> 00:30:57,431
Can we not talk about this now?
Can we change the subject?

417
00:30:57,501 --> 00:30:59,093
Do you understand?

418
00:30:59,170 --> 00:31:01,764
We want a pool.

419
00:31:05,843 --> 00:31:08,203
- You're tellin' me later.
- I'll tell you everything later.

420
00:31:08,212 --> 00:31:10,806
Look at those guys out there.

421
00:31:10,881 --> 00:31:15,147
They're laughing,
they're all happy...

422
00:31:15,219 --> 00:31:18,245
and waving to their friends.

423
00:31:18,322 --> 00:31:21,257
But the next day... and this is
the thing they don't know...

424
00:31:21,325 --> 00:31:24,522
they could be lying on the slab.

425
00:31:24,595 --> 00:31:27,587
It's kind of harsh.

426
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:31,300
But it's kind of fun too.

427
00:31:36,173 --> 00:31:38,437
- Do you ever...
- What?

428
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:42,800
Well, you know.

429
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,300
Are you tempted to, like...

430
00:31:48,500 --> 00:31:51,400
wanna fool around with the bodies?

431
00:31:51,889 --> 00:31:54,050
No, I've always wanted to ask.

432
00:31:54,125 --> 00:31:56,059
I'm sorry if
it makes you uncomfortable.

433
00:31:56,127 --> 00:31:59,563
- People are curious about that.
- If you don't wanna talk about it...

434
00:31:59,630 --> 00:32:03,031
The worst thing that we do is
we take the grotesque bodies...

435
00:32:03,100 --> 00:32:05,830
the really ugly ones...

436
00:32:05,903 --> 00:32:09,498
and we make
harmless jokes about them.

437
00:32:09,573 --> 00:32:12,303
Very harmless jokes,
but we come up with...

438
00:32:12,376 --> 00:32:15,675
some very good jokes about them...

439
00:32:15,746 --> 00:32:17,907
my father and me.

440
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:20,400
But, you know, they're dead.

441
00:32:21,700 --> 00:32:24,400
- Nobody hears anything.
- Hi, boys.

442
00:32:24,588 --> 00:32:27,056
Hello, Mrs. Carver.

443
00:32:27,124 --> 00:32:29,922
Those jokes don't hurt anybody.
Nobody knows we even make them.

444
00:32:29,993 --> 00:32:32,860
Gilbert, I'm waiting for your call.

445
00:32:32,930 --> 00:32:36,058
Mr. Carver, I haven't seen
your mother in church lately.

446
00:32:36,133 --> 00:32:38,226
- How's she doing?
- She's fine.

447
00:32:38,302 --> 00:32:41,100
Thanks. Bye.

448
00:32:41,171 --> 00:32:43,731
He wants to kill you, right?

449
00:32:43,807 --> 00:32:47,174
Do you prefer a bronze casket?

450
00:33:09,967 --> 00:33:12,128
Can somebody give me
a hand down here?

451
00:33:12,202 --> 00:33:15,467
- What?
- I need a hand with the wood.

452
00:33:20,900 --> 00:33:23,000
You wanna go help Tucker?

453
00:33:25,800 --> 00:33:28,400
Go help Tucker in the basement.

454
00:33:34,458 --> 00:33:37,757
- Go into the basement...
- I don't wanna go down there.

455
00:33:37,828 --> 00:33:41,594
- Please?
- No way! No way! You!

456
00:33:41,700 --> 00:33:45,600
- Go down there, Gilbert.
- Is there a problem?

457
00:33:48,472 --> 00:33:51,635
Dad's in there!

458
00:33:59,149 --> 00:34:00,741
Shut up!

459
00:34:14,231 --> 00:34:15,823
Come on!

460
00:34:23,040 --> 00:34:24,940
It's not funny!

461
00:34:25,008 --> 00:34:26,600
Get back here!

462
00:34:30,948 --> 00:34:33,678
Don't worry.
Those are two-by-sixes.

463
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:37,700
There's six of'em,
so those could hold anybody.

464
00:34:46,463 --> 00:34:48,055
- I forgot.
- What?

465
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:54,700
I forgot that
that was where your dad...

466
00:34:59,676 --> 00:35:01,268
I'm sorry.

467
00:35:03,200 --> 00:35:06,300
No, that's okay.
Don't worry about it.

468
00:35:13,123 --> 00:35:16,024
- No, Arnie! No climbing!
- I wanna go up there!

469
00:35:16,093 --> 00:35:17,390
No, you're not!

470
00:35:19,663 --> 00:35:21,290
Not again!

471
00:35:21,365 --> 00:35:23,925
- I wanna go up there!
- Get down. Get down.

472
00:35:24,001 --> 00:35:25,468
Get down!

473
00:35:28,238 --> 00:35:31,867
You're not going anywhere!
Not too much fun, is it?

474
00:35:31,942 --> 00:35:34,172
I wanna go up there!

475
00:35:41,418 --> 00:35:43,010
We're going home.

476
00:35:44,521 --> 00:35:46,546
- Stop!
- Ellen, no!

477
00:35:46,623 --> 00:35:48,955
Stop it!
I told you, don't touch him.

478
00:35:49,026 --> 00:35:51,017
- Don't ever touch him again.
- He was climbing again!

479
00:35:51,094 --> 00:35:54,530
I don't care.
Just get out of here!

480
00:35:54,600 --> 00:35:57,800
Let me see, buddy.
Come on. Let me see.

481
00:35:58,800 --> 00:36:01,300
Oh, great.
You made him bleed!

482
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:05,508
What does Gilbert say?

483
00:36:05,575 --> 00:36:08,009
If anybody ever hits you...

484
00:36:08,100 --> 00:36:12,800
or even just lays a finger on you,
what are you gonna do?

485
00:36:15,686 --> 00:36:19,679
You're gonna tell me, and then
I'm gonna take care of it for you.

486
00:36:19,800 --> 00:36:22,400
And why will I take care of it?

487
00:36:24,528 --> 00:36:27,053
- Because you're Gilbert.
- Because I'm Gilbert.

488
00:36:27,200 --> 00:36:30,000
Because nobody hurts Arnie,
right?

489
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:34,500
You wanna pick out some candy?

490
00:36:40,444 --> 00:36:43,038
- Can I talk to you for a minute?
- What do you want?

491
00:36:43,113 --> 00:36:45,775
We've got to keep
a closer eye on him.

492
00:36:45,849 --> 00:36:48,750
- What?
- We've gotta do better.

493
00:36:48,900 --> 00:36:50,900
Are you listening to me?

494
00:36:54,691 --> 00:36:55,817
Mine.

495
00:36:55,892 --> 00:36:59,328
And you.
You have to stay here.

496
00:36:59,396 --> 00:37:02,695
You stay right on this porch.
You don't go anywhere.

497
00:37:02,766 --> 00:37:06,793
- Don't go anywhere.
- Don't go anywhere.

498
00:37:06,900 --> 00:37:09,000
We're not going anywhere.

499
00:37:31,962 --> 00:37:33,725
Where are you going?

500
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:42,600
I'm waiting.
Waitin' for that call, Gilbert.

501
00:38:57,581 --> 00:38:59,515
- Look. Come here.
- What?

502
00:38:59,583 --> 00:39:02,347
It's a praying mantis.

503
00:39:02,419 --> 00:39:06,321
You know how they mate? The male
will sneak up on the female...

504
00:39:06,390 --> 00:39:08,449
and she'll bite off his head...

505
00:39:08,525 --> 00:39:10,993
and the rest of his body
will keep on mating.

506
00:39:11,061 --> 00:39:13,222
And then when they're done...

507
00:39:13,297 --> 00:39:15,322
she'll eat him.

508
00:39:15,400 --> 00:39:17,700
She'll eat the rest of him.

509
00:39:18,569 --> 00:39:22,938
Grandma, we have company.
So, do you want to eat?

510
00:39:25,900 --> 00:39:28,300
- Help yourself.
- Thank you.

511
00:39:32,300 --> 00:39:35,600
Well, we missed the rally
in Des Moines.

512
00:39:36,854 --> 00:39:38,788
If we get on the road by Friday,
we'll be able...

513
00:39:38,856 --> 00:39:41,723
to make Colorado Springs
in time to catch them.

514
00:39:41,792 --> 00:39:43,760
Have you ever been to Colorado?

515
00:39:43,827 --> 00:39:45,692
No, ma'am.

516
00:39:45,763 --> 00:39:47,663
It must be wonderful.

517
00:39:47,731 --> 00:39:49,756
It must be incredibly
frustrating then...

518
00:39:49,833 --> 00:39:52,324
to be stuck here in this place,
in Endora.

519
00:39:52,403 --> 00:39:55,167
This place
is as good a place as any.

520
00:39:55,239 --> 00:39:57,537
Think so?

521
00:39:57,608 --> 00:39:59,098
She should know.

522
00:39:59,943 --> 00:40:02,605
Becky's been just about
everywhere there is to go.

523
00:40:02,679 --> 00:40:04,613
Places I didn't even know existed.

524
00:40:04,681 --> 00:40:07,878
I'm a worldly kind of girl.

525
00:40:09,920 --> 00:40:14,289
Me, I spent most of my whole life
in the same spot.

526
00:40:14,358 --> 00:40:16,622
Why doesn't matter.

527
00:40:16,693 --> 00:40:20,288
Anyway, she encouraged me
to get out.

528
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:23,100
Now she can't stay put anywhere.

529
00:40:25,803 --> 00:40:29,000
She's the smartest,
most beautiful girl in the world.

530
00:40:29,072 --> 00:40:31,040
Isn't she beautiful?

531
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:40,207
I'm sorry. She has this thing
with beauty that...

532
00:40:40,284 --> 00:40:42,752
Yeah, I noticed that.

533
00:40:42,820 --> 00:40:47,154
I'm not into that...
that whole external beauty thing.

534
00:40:47,224 --> 00:40:50,660
- 'Cause it doesn't last.
- Right.

535
00:40:50,727 --> 00:40:54,163
Eventually, your face
is gonna get wrinkly...

536
00:40:54,231 --> 00:40:57,826
you'll get gray hair,
your boobs might sag.

537
00:40:57,901 --> 00:41:00,199
You know? So what?

538
00:41:00,270 --> 00:41:03,262
It's what you do
that really matters.

539
00:41:03,340 --> 00:41:05,900
- Right?
- Yeah, sure.

540
00:41:05,976 --> 00:41:08,069
So what do you wanna do?

541
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:14,200
I don't know. There's not
so much to do here, really.

542
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:19,500
You can think of one thing.
Think of one thing people do here.

543
00:41:23,527 --> 00:41:25,586
Thank you.

544
00:41:25,700 --> 00:41:27,700
It was nice meeting you.

545
00:41:29,867 --> 00:41:30,925
Be nice.

546
00:41:46,100 --> 00:41:50,100
Can I have yours
and I'll give you mine instead?

547
00:41:50,654 --> 00:41:52,315
We want the big one!

548
00:41:52,389 --> 00:41:54,949
You know something?
The one on top of it is fine.

549
00:41:55,025 --> 00:41:58,085
We want the big one!

550
00:42:00,063 --> 00:42:02,122
- Let's go.
- Get us the big one!

551
00:42:02,199 --> 00:42:05,168
- Come on, Mom. Please?
- Here you go, guys.

552
00:42:05,300 --> 00:42:08,800
- We want the big one.
- Yeah, that's fine.

553
00:42:09,873 --> 00:42:11,773
It's changing.

554
00:42:11,842 --> 00:42:14,310
That's what's wild about the sunset.

555
00:42:14,400 --> 00:42:19,500
It'll just change really,
really slowly in front of your eyes.

556
00:42:24,922 --> 00:42:27,288
I love the sky.

557
00:42:27,357 --> 00:42:31,418
It's so limitless.

558
00:42:32,563 --> 00:42:35,361
It is big.
It's very big.

559
00:42:35,432 --> 00:42:37,332
Big doesn't even sum it up right.

560
00:42:37,401 --> 00:42:39,198
That word "big" is so small.

561
00:42:39,269 --> 00:42:42,796
You'd have to get
those really giant words...

562
00:42:42,873 --> 00:42:45,307
to describe the sky.

563
00:42:49,880 --> 00:42:51,541
What?

564
00:42:53,100 --> 00:42:57,000
I have to go do this thing.
It's kind of a family thing.

565
00:42:57,154 --> 00:43:00,282
Do you want me to give you a ride
back into town, or do you wanna...

566
00:43:00,400 --> 00:43:03,500
No, actually,
I'm just gonna sit here.

567
00:43:07,631 --> 00:43:10,759
I could come back.
I mean, I can come back and...

568
00:43:10,834 --> 00:43:13,359
- Really?
- Yeah. You'll be here then?

569
00:43:13,437 --> 00:43:15,530
Yeah. I'll just sit here.

570
00:43:15,700 --> 00:43:19,000
All right, I'll be back
in a little bit.

571
00:43:23,300 --> 00:43:26,000
Hey, buddy. Come on.
We gotta go.

572
00:43:29,620 --> 00:43:32,214
Where's the duck?
I can't see the duck anywhere.

573
00:43:32,289 --> 00:43:35,520
- Find him. Look. Where'd he go?
- Where's the duck?

574
00:43:35,592 --> 00:43:39,050
- It's hiding. Find the duck.
- I don't have time for this.

575
00:43:39,129 --> 00:43:41,427
Lift up. Okay, good.

576
00:43:41,498 --> 00:43:44,626
- Ducky.
- Good boy. You know what?

577
00:43:44,701 --> 00:43:47,169
- You're such a big boy.
- Yeah.

578
00:43:47,237 --> 00:43:49,467
- You're such a big boy.
- I'm a big boy.

579
00:43:49,600 --> 00:43:54,200
I bet you could do this all
by yourself if you really wanted to.

580
00:43:54,378 --> 00:43:56,676
- Could you do this by yourself?
- I'm a big boy.

581
00:43:56,747 --> 00:43:58,806
- Yeah, be a big boy.
- Big boy.

582
00:43:58,882 --> 00:44:01,715
Take this, wash everything.

583
00:44:01,785 --> 00:44:05,915
Your towels are there,
and your robe is there.

584
00:44:05,989 --> 00:44:09,516
- The big boy's gonna wash himself.
- Right.

585
00:44:09,593 --> 00:44:11,720
- I gotta go.
- Okay.

586
00:44:14,097 --> 00:44:17,089
- You missed it.
- What did I miss?

587
00:44:17,167 --> 00:44:19,499
- The sunset.
- Really?

588
00:44:19,569 --> 00:44:22,094
It was beautiful.

589
00:44:22,172 --> 00:44:23,764
Oh, well.

590
00:44:27,644 --> 00:44:30,738
I'd like to see where you live.

591
00:44:30,814 --> 00:44:32,372
No, you wouldn't.

592
00:44:32,449 --> 00:44:34,713
Let's go see where you live.

593
00:44:34,785 --> 00:44:36,377
Come on.

594
00:44:43,300 --> 00:44:46,300
My parents split up
when I was a kid.

595
00:44:47,297 --> 00:44:49,629
I go back and forth between them...

596
00:44:49,700 --> 00:44:52,200
'cause they're always moving.

597
00:44:52,702 --> 00:44:55,899
But it's good.
It's my life.

598
00:44:59,742 --> 00:45:01,869
We don't really move.

599
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:04,400
I mean, we'd like to, but...

600
00:45:05,700 --> 00:45:09,000
my mom is sort of
attached to the house.

601
00:45:09,652 --> 00:45:12,246
Attached is, I guess,
not the right word.

602
00:45:12,322 --> 00:45:14,688
She's pretty much wedged in.

603
00:45:14,757 --> 00:45:18,090
- What do you mean?
- That's it.

604
00:45:18,200 --> 00:45:19,700
That's the house.

605
00:45:22,298 --> 00:45:24,391
It's really amazing.

606
00:45:24,500 --> 00:45:29,100
I mean, how small it looks
from here, considering the...

607
00:45:29,200 --> 00:45:32,000
the girth of what's inside of it.

608
00:45:36,846 --> 00:45:39,144
I don't know.

609
00:45:39,300 --> 00:45:43,200
Did you ever see
a beached whale on television?

610
00:45:44,754 --> 00:45:47,723
That's her.
That's my mom.

611
00:45:52,829 --> 00:45:54,763
What about your dad?

612
00:45:55,898 --> 00:45:59,197
Some other day.
Some other day.

613
00:46:12,649 --> 00:46:15,243
I had a nice time tonight.

614
00:46:17,053 --> 00:46:19,317
I know.

615
00:46:22,400 --> 00:46:24,600
- Good night.
- Good night.

616
00:47:13,500 --> 00:47:15,800
Come on.
I'm sorry. Come on.

617
00:47:18,681 --> 00:47:20,672
Here. You're okay.

618
00:47:25,054 --> 00:47:26,783
Come on. Get warm.

619
00:47:26,856 --> 00:47:30,348
Oh, God, I'm sorry.
I'm sorry, buddy.

620
00:47:30,426 --> 00:47:34,123
I'm so sorry.
I'm sorry.

621
00:47:34,197 --> 00:47:37,826
- Would somebody please explain?
- Gilbert's in charge of bathing.

622
00:47:37,900 --> 00:47:40,164
I could have "drownded."

623
00:47:43,172 --> 00:47:45,572
- No more baths.
- But you didn't, honey.

624
00:47:45,700 --> 00:47:49,700
- You could've, but you didn't.
- No more baths.

625
00:47:51,600 --> 00:47:55,400
It is too much to ask
to see this boy turn 18?

626
00:47:56,319 --> 00:47:57,513
It's ready.

627
00:47:57,587 --> 00:48:00,078
Where's your head lately?

628
00:48:00,156 --> 00:48:02,920
Where is your head?

629
00:48:04,160 --> 00:48:07,652
- Sorry, Mama.
- Sorry isn't good enough.

630
00:48:07,730 --> 00:48:09,823
You gotta do better.

631
00:48:09,899 --> 00:48:11,958
Gotta do better.

632
00:48:14,300 --> 00:48:17,300
Hey, boss, is that the right price?

633
00:48:18,207 --> 00:48:20,232
That's right.

634
00:48:20,309 --> 00:48:24,006
- It seems like it ought to be more.
- Maybe at Foodland.

635
00:48:24,080 --> 00:48:27,413
We've always had
a reasonable deal on pickles.

636
00:48:27,483 --> 00:48:28,916
Here.

637
00:48:31,554 --> 00:48:33,579
Gilbert, got a delivery
for you, son.

638
00:48:33,656 --> 00:48:35,248
It sounds urgent.

639
00:48:46,436 --> 00:48:49,234
Get out.
Go outside and play, right now.

640
00:48:49,305 --> 00:48:51,569
Right now. Hurry up.

641
00:48:59,900 --> 00:49:01,400
- Hi, Betty.
- Hi.

642
00:49:04,387 --> 00:49:06,981
Could you dial that number
over there for me?

643
00:49:07,056 --> 00:49:10,583
- My hands are all...
- Yeah, sure.

644
00:49:10,660 --> 00:49:12,628
- How have you been?
- Good.

645
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:14,500
I saw you last night.

646
00:49:16,165 --> 00:49:17,928
Who's the girl?

647
00:49:19,001 --> 00:49:22,368
- It's ringing.
- Sorry. One sec.

648
00:49:24,100 --> 00:49:25,800
This is good. Taste.

649
00:49:26,742 --> 00:49:28,209
That's good. It's ringing.

650
00:49:28,277 --> 00:49:30,541
One second.

651
00:49:31,600 --> 00:49:35,000
Hello? Ken Carver here,
Carver Insurance.

652
00:49:39,989 --> 00:49:42,856
- Mr. Carver?
- Who is this?

653
00:49:42,925 --> 00:49:44,358
It's Gilbert.

654
00:49:46,762 --> 00:49:49,595
I'd given up on you, Gilbert.

655
00:49:49,700 --> 00:49:53,200
- Did you?
- Well, yeah. Can you blame me?

656
00:49:53,302 --> 00:49:56,760
I mean, how many times do I have
to ask, and still no visit?

657
00:49:56,839 --> 00:49:59,865
- Well, I'm here now.
- Happy anniversary.

658
00:49:59,942 --> 00:50:02,206
Well, we can't discuss this
over the phone. I think it's best...

659
00:50:02,278 --> 00:50:05,111
that we meet man to man,
don't you agree?

660
00:50:05,181 --> 00:50:07,547
- Yes.
- Today is your lucky day.

661
00:50:07,700 --> 00:50:13,100
I've just had a cancellation.
What about right now? Are you free?

662
00:50:14,457 --> 00:50:15,924
Is that a yes?

663
00:50:17,927 --> 00:50:19,258
- Okay.
- All right.

664
00:50:19,400 --> 00:50:22,300
I'm gonna be waiting here for you.

665
00:50:23,866 --> 00:50:27,267
Do you want me to be killed?
Do you want him to kill me?

666
00:50:27,336 --> 00:50:30,499
Just playing.
Don't you wanna play?

667
00:50:30,573 --> 00:50:32,006
This is crazy.

668
00:50:32,074 --> 00:50:34,872
- I've gotta go.
- You don't have to go.

669
00:50:34,944 --> 00:50:36,172
Yes, I do.

670
00:50:39,849 --> 00:50:42,317
It's that new girl, isn't it?

671
00:50:42,400 --> 00:50:46,100
It's your husband. He wants me
to come to his office right now.

672
00:50:46,222 --> 00:50:49,248
If you walk out that door...

673
00:50:49,400 --> 00:50:52,300
Don't you dare walk out that door.

674
00:51:16,200 --> 00:51:18,400
You look nervous, Gilbert.

675
00:51:19,600 --> 00:51:22,400
I'd be nervous too if I were you.

676
00:51:22,900 --> 00:51:27,400
If I were in your situation,
I'd be downright panicky.

677
00:51:27,830 --> 00:51:30,526
I reviewed your file.

678
00:51:30,600 --> 00:51:33,700
You've got
no major medical insurance.

679
00:51:33,936 --> 00:51:36,666
No catastrophic, no life.

680
00:51:41,100 --> 00:51:44,400
What if something
were to happen to you?

681
00:51:44,913 --> 00:51:47,473
Something unforeseeable?

682
00:51:47,549 --> 00:51:50,143
Something sudden? Random?

683
00:51:51,553 --> 00:51:55,182
An accident, maybe.
What about your family?

684
00:51:57,200 --> 00:52:00,200
Do you ever think about your family?

685
00:52:01,100 --> 00:52:05,000
Stop thinking about yourself.
Think about them.

686
00:52:05,267 --> 00:52:09,328
You don't wanna leave 'em
empty-handed.

687
00:52:09,404 --> 00:52:12,066
Ken Carver here.

688
00:52:12,200 --> 00:52:15,200
Can't this wait?
I'm in the middle...

689
00:52:16,912 --> 00:52:19,506
Please, calm down.
Calm down.

690
00:52:22,751 --> 00:52:23,945
Go on.

691
00:52:41,169 --> 00:52:43,603
Calm... I'm on my way.

692
00:52:49,000 --> 00:52:52,500
Troubles at home.
I'm sure you understand.

693
00:52:52,848 --> 00:52:55,214
Damn. Betty's got the car.

694
00:52:55,284 --> 00:52:58,253
Would you give me a ride?

695
00:53:19,074 --> 00:53:21,304
Oh, my God! Betty!

696
00:53:21,376 --> 00:53:23,537
What the hell's going on here?

697
00:53:23,612 --> 00:53:26,012
Todd? Doug?
What is going on here?

698
00:53:26,081 --> 00:53:28,015
I don't believe this!

699
00:53:30,052 --> 00:53:31,644
Oh, great!

700
00:53:34,356 --> 00:53:35,948
Boys, come on.

701
00:53:36,100 --> 00:53:40,000
Let's go show your mom the cookies
that she's baked for us.

702
00:53:40,195 --> 00:53:41,662
This is great.

703
00:53:44,100 --> 00:53:46,500
All right.
Everything's okay.

704
00:53:49,171 --> 00:53:52,629
Look, honey, they're fine.
They taste fine.

705
00:53:52,708 --> 00:53:55,472
They're a little burnt on top,
but just fine.

706
00:53:55,544 --> 00:53:58,445
They're wonderful.

707
00:53:58,513 --> 00:54:01,380
Boys, here.
Have some of Mom's cookies.

708
00:54:01,450 --> 00:54:03,281
They're really good.

709
00:54:03,352 --> 00:54:05,513
Come on, boys.
Make your mother happy.

710
00:54:05,600 --> 00:54:08,800
Make your mom happy.
Have some cookies.

711
00:54:12,527 --> 00:54:16,054
I could've had any guy.
Any guy!

712
00:54:16,131 --> 00:54:18,361
But...

713
00:54:18,433 --> 00:54:20,458
I chose you.

714
00:54:21,903 --> 00:54:24,201
I got you a real pool,
for God's sake!

715
00:54:24,272 --> 00:54:26,832
Look! There's water in here!

716
00:54:26,908 --> 00:54:29,399
Come here!
Get over here!

717
00:54:30,779 --> 00:54:32,246
Get inside the pool!

718
00:54:32,314 --> 00:54:35,249
Get inside the pool
with your brother!

719
00:54:35,317 --> 00:54:37,080
Why did you?

720
00:54:37,152 --> 00:54:40,781
Yeah. Look.
Real water, boys.

721
00:54:43,425 --> 00:54:46,326
Because...

722
00:54:46,400 --> 00:54:48,900
I knew you'd always be there.

723
00:54:50,699 --> 00:54:53,167
Because I knew you'd never leave.

724
00:54:53,235 --> 00:54:56,363
What the hell else
more do you want?

725
00:54:56,438 --> 00:54:59,134
What? For God's sake!

726
00:55:01,600 --> 00:55:05,600
Son, get back in the pool.
Get back in the pool!

727
00:55:06,682 --> 00:55:09,617
We're all gonna enjoy it!
It's a lot of fun, isn't it?

728
00:55:09,700 --> 00:55:14,100
I'm doin' the best I can here.
I can't do any better!

729
00:55:14,200 --> 00:55:18,200
I can't give anymore.
I've given enough already.

730
00:55:29,504 --> 00:55:31,529
I guess maybe
I'd better be getting off.

731
00:55:31,606 --> 00:55:32,732
Not yet.

732
00:55:34,710 --> 00:55:37,645
Arthur, in all my life...

733
00:55:37,713 --> 00:55:40,773
I'll wonder, where is he?

734
00:55:42,818 --> 00:55:45,981
Just this moment, just now...

735
00:55:47,489 --> 00:55:50,151
what is he looking at?

736
00:55:50,225 --> 00:55:51,715
What is he thinking?

737
00:55:51,800 --> 00:55:55,300
I think it's time for Arnie
to take a bath.

738
00:55:57,199 --> 00:56:00,327
Don't you think it's time
for Arnie to take a bath, Gilbert?

739
00:56:00,402 --> 00:56:02,666
Just let him stink.

740
00:56:02,738 --> 00:56:05,901
- I don't wanna take a bath!
- Please.

741
00:56:05,974 --> 00:56:08,670
You know Mr. Carver?

742
00:56:09,811 --> 00:56:11,403
Well, he's dead.

743
00:56:39,100 --> 00:56:41,700
- What's going on?
- He drowned.

744
00:56:43,700 --> 00:56:46,300
- You're kidding?
- No. In that.

745
00:56:49,100 --> 00:56:51,600
A kiddie pool.
I don't get it.

